{"reference":"Judges 14","book":"Judges","chapter":14,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Samson within Judges","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Samson’s story is introduced as the beginning, rather than the completion, of Israel’s deliverance from Philistine rule. That larger storyline continues beyond this chapter, so Judges 14 should be read as an opening movement in Samson’s conflict with the Philistines, not as a self-contained resolution.","verse_refs":["Judges 13:1-25","Judges 15:1-20","Judges 16:1-31"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_judges_014_22b41b9ac71e59aa390d8092"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"},{"id":"block_2","text":"The recurring pattern introduced earlier in Judges helps frame its central narratives, but the individual episodes do not follow every stage in a mechanically identical way. Samson’s story therefore belongs within that larger pattern while retaining its own distinctive course.","verse_refs":["Judges 1","Judges 10:1-18","Judges 11:1-40","Judges 12:1-15","Judges 13:1-25","Judges 15:1-20","Judges 16:1-31","Judges 2:1-23","Judges 3:1-31","Judges 3:7-31","Judges 4:1-24","Judges 5:1-31","Judges 6:1-40","Judges 7:1-25","Judges 8:1-35","Judges 9:1-57"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_judges_014_2efe995c6b600a381d73a2f4"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}